WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.940
$80 billion is Samsung's estimated quarter, topping Nvidia's last operating profit. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, episode 17. Euro news has Samsung's Thursday estimate at 107.4 trillion WAN, which it converts as $80.2 billion, or $71.5 billion Euros. That is up from 89.49 trillion WAN in the previous quarter, and from 12.17 trillion WAN a year earlier.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:35.360
The year-on-year jump works out to 782.5%.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.440
If the number holds, Euro news says it would be the largest quarterly operating profit

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.740
a technology company has ever reported, and the first time a South Korean firms quarterly

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.520
operating profit cleared 100 trillion won.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:57.200
LSEG had the analyst consensus at 106.1 trillion won, so the estimate landed just above that.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:07.480
Sales are estimated at $195 trillion, $145.6 billion, up 127% from a year ago.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:12.180
That implies an operating margin of about 55%.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.840
Samsung did not split the estimate by division.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:21.440
Euro news ties the print to AI data centers buying high bandwidth memory, with tight supply

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.160
also pushing DRAM and NAND prices up.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:29.480
up. The full results, including that missing split, are scheduled for the 29th of October.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:39.400
The stock still closed 2.42% lower at 262,000 won, and the cost be fell 2.62% as holders

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:45.460
took profits. AMD says sixth-generation EPIC processors will power the next generation

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:51.800
of HPE ProLiant servers, and it calls those machines built for the AI era. The post

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.620
names the processor generation and the server family and stops there.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:02.240
Dylan Patel of semi-analysis says together AI was downgraded in cluster max over reliability

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.340
and quality and that the problems were not confined to a single site.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:12.500
He says Nebius had much less downtime and that every cloud has some outage, the useful

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.760
question is how much and how often.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:21.680
In a separate post he says semi-analysis never asked iron or any cloud to pay for coverage

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:28.660
or for a ranking. TSMC's own third quarter print is now in and seeking alpha puts record

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:37.480
revenue at $1.49 trillion new Taiwan dollars, $46.71 billion US dollars. That is up 50% year

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:44.740
on year and it clears the LSEG smart estimate of $1.46 trillion new Taiwan dollars. Trading

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:51.240
King Key, adding the monthly figures, gets about 1.494 trillion new Taiwan dollars, roughly

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.740
$46.8 billion US dollars.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:03:01.580
Either way the quarter sits above the range TSMC itself had guided, $44.6 to $45.8 billion.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:10.520
September alone was $511.86 billion new Taiwan dollars, about $16.07 billion US dollars.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:18.780
That September figure is up 54.6% from September 2025 and down 0.6% from August.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:29.700
January through September totals, $3.898.73 billion new Taiwan dollars, about $122.42 billion US dollars,

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.520
up 41.1% year-on-year.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:38.700
A Reuters analyst survey cited by Trading Key looks for third quarter net profit around

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.820
$740.8 billion new Taiwan dollars, up about 64 percent.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.100
That is an outside estimate, not a TSMC result.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:53.320
The company's earlier margin guide for the quarter was a gross margin of 65 to 67 percent,

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.920
and an operating margin of 56 to 58 percent.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:01.020
The full report and the earnings conference are on the 15th of October.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:10.100
Rome is widening outsourced assembly and tests in India, while it keeps wafer fabrication inside its own fabs, e.e. Times reports.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:19.960
Managing director Makoto Tarada told the paper Tata Electronics gets TOL packages, and Suchi Semicon gets T0252.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:28.420
TOL, he said, is widely used on two wheelers, and the main T0252 base is more like four wheelers.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:32.000
The first parts through those lines will be power MOSFETs.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:37.080
Legacy products Rome has built for a long time, so the company can see whether the new

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.980
partners can package a known die.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.760
Terada said the focus stays analog and power, and he did not point to advance packaging

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.160
in India at this stage.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:51.640
He also said both partners could later run the same package types, but only if demand

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.400
supports it.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:57.880
The point of the trial is local production first, then a possible stretch to global demand

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.020
and once the partners are benchmarked.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.100
Semi-conductor engineering describes advanced packaging

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.440
as cost that stacks layer by layer,

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.340
component by component, step by step.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.680
By the time chiplets high-band with memory stacks

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.160
or hybrid bonded devices reach assembly,

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.880
the material and the process time are spent.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.740
A defect found there threatens the assembly,

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.620
not a die that can still be scrapped at the front end.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.860
The failures are not one shape.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:31.600
The piece names Surface Particles, Cracks, Embedded Defects, Irregular Microbumps, and Bonding

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:35.920
Voids, and it says Bump Height and Surface Profile still have to be measured.

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:41.820
A camera aimed at the top face can catch a particle on a pad and still miss a void inside

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:42.320
the bond.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.840
High Sensitivity to Dimensional Inspection is for Surface Particles and Pattern Anomalies.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:53.400
High Speed Infrared is for Voids and Embedded Defects a visible light tool never sees.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:59.140
3-dimensional metrology is what separates a short bump from a dirty one, by measuring

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.180
height and profile.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.700
Hybrid bonding and fine pitch bumps have pulled package tolerances toward the range once

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.460
reserved for front and fabrication.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:14.020
Multi-angle illumination is described as the way sidewall and low contrast defects show

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:17.220
up when ordinary bright field or dark field misses them.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:22.840
A second note, the same day puts electrical process control next to that optical stack,

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:26.620
because a bond can look closed and still fail as a connection.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:33.180
If the inspection step is too slow, it becomes the bottleneck on a line that is already capital-intensive.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:38.980
Complementary optical, infrared, and height checks stop being the right gate when the only

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:44.000
tools that can see the void cannot match the assembly rate, and the line either waits

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.920
on inspection or ship stacks whose internal bonds were never measured.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:54.420
On the horizon, the 15th of October is TSMC's full third quarter report and conference,

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:00.600
where trading key says the watch items are capacity utilization, gross margin, and demand

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.440
guidance for the fourth quarter of 2026 and for 2027.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:09.200
The 29th of October is Samsung's full third quarter publication.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.880
The date Euro news gives for the division split Thursday's estimate left out.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:20.520
Before we go, the nearest date on that list is the 15th of October, when TSMC's quarterly

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:24.000
revenue print becomes a full set of margins and a forward guide.

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:27.120
That's AI Chips and Data Centers for today.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.960
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

